hub.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T00:46:53Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T00:46:53Z","body":"IMO the icons for Verbose and Recovery Mode are helpful because they are the same overall action (opening the project in the editor) but are different *variants* of it, and the icons help emphasize that.\r\n\r\nAs shown in my comment above, Godot includes icons for \"copy\", \"rename\", and \"duplicate\" actions in other areas, so I think it'd be strange to omit them here. In general, I feel like the choices of items here to have icons versus not is rather arbitrary.\r\n\r\nPerhaps there could be a proposal or discussion in the future over whether the use of icons in context menus should be toned down across Godot (including this menu), but for now I think the icons provided for each item fit and have precedent with the rest of the editor's design.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3530340855/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3530603226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112733#issuecomment-3530603226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112733","id":3530603226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ScLra","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","a